[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged on subject lines ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject))
and marked known as one parser bug. Read for what each report shows, it holds three problems.
Each one now has a ticket of its own.

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} issues={{ parser: `${repo}/1`, hint: `${repo}/2`, 'one-day': `${repo}/3` }} />

<Callout kind="warn">
The queued parser fix closes only the <code>parser</code> row. The other two keep coming after it ships.
</Callout>

## How a report is placed

1. **`one-day`**: the date moved by one day, not month for day ("Lisbon got Tuesday, Toronto got
   Monday"). This is time zones, not the parser. The desk already listed these reports in `desk-notes.json`.
2. **`hint`**: the report came through the booking form of a tenant on `booking-v3`. The form's hint says
   `MM/DD/YYYY`, people type month first, and the form reads the date day first.
3. **`parser`**: every other report from a day-first tenant. The shared parser reads the date month first.

The tenant decides the problem, not the reporter's browser. Intake tags from the browser, so its tag
is wrong in the reports counted in the table.

## For the desk

- Keep #4471 for `parser` only. Move new `hint` and `one-day` reports to their own tickets.
- Subjects do not tell these apart: the same subject line shows up under all three problems. Merging on
  subject needs a new decision record to replace 0001.

